msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Closing her eyes, she called out to the spirit."
msgstr "Cerrando los ojos, le llamó al espíritu."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Razaphel."
msgstr "Razafael."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "When she opened her eyes again, she saw the creature floating in the room."
msgstr "Cuando volvió a abrir los ojos, vio a la criatura flotando en la habitación."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Sarah..."
msgstr "Sarah..."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "He spoke her name with hissing breath, slowly."
msgstr "Ella pronunció su nombre con un aliento siseante, lentamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The creature's body, black as ink in its center, frayed off like mist to its edges."
msgstr "El cuerpo de la criatura, negro como la tinta en su centro, se desvanecía como niebla hacia sus bordes."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was always hard to grasp the spirit's shape, if it even had such a thing as a true form."
msgstr "Siempre había sido difícil captar la forma del espíritu, si es que siquiera tenía una forma verdadera."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "You summoned me?"
msgstr "¿Me has invocado?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "For a moment, the spirit was silent. It's pale mask facing her."
msgstr "Por un momento, el espíritu guardó silencio. Su pálida máscara estaba orientada hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was as close a thing as the creature had to a face."
msgstr "Era lo más parecido a un rostro que la criatura tenía."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Why?"
msgstr "¿Por qué?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The rhythm of it's voice was strangely melodic."
msgstr "El ritmo de su voz era extrañamente melódico."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah wondered about what to say. She wasn't entirely sure herself."
msgstr "Sarah se preguntaba qué decir. Ella misma no estaba del todo segura."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "I didn't want to be alone."
msgstr "No quería estar sola."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The spirit slowly drifted through the air like smoke from a pipe."
msgstr "El espíritu flotaba lentamente por el aire como el humo de una pipa."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Surely, you are not short in friends."
msgstr "Seguro que no te faltan amigos."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "An army waits outside these gates."
msgstr "Un ejército espera fuera de estas puertas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah studied the spirit."
msgstr "Sarah estudió al espíritu."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Soldiers are not friends."
msgstr "Los soldados no son amigos."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "True. But I am sure you have some you could call on?"
msgstr "Cierto. Pero estoy seguro de que tienes a algunos en los que podrías confiar, ¿no?"

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "It was true, but still she had decided on the spirit."
msgstr "Era cierto, pero aun así había decidido confiar en el espíritu."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yes...but I called on you."
msgstr "Sí... pero recurrí a ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Because I am your best friend?"
msgstr "¿Porque soy tu mejor amigo?"

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Or rather because you're not a friend at all."
msgstr "O más bien, porque en realidad no eres un amigo para nada."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The spirit's body flinched."
msgstr "El cuerpo del espíritu se estremeció."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "You wound me."
msgstr "Me hieres."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You're right, I am not short people that might answer my summons."
msgstr "Tienes razón, no soy una persona que se deje intimidar fácilmente."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "But they are loyal. They tell me what I want to hear. Not always what I need to hear."
msgstr "Pero son leales. Me dicen lo que quiero oír. No siempre lo que necesito oír."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "You never seem to tell me what I want to hear."
msgstr "Nunca pareces decirme lo que quiero oír."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "A soft hissing laugh emerged from the spirit."
msgstr "Una risa suave y sibilante surgió del espíritu."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "No, I have been accused of many things."
msgstr "No, me han acusado de muchas cosas."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Helpful has not been one of them."
msgstr "Ser útil no ha sido una de ellas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah frowned. It frustrated her how much the spirit enjoyed its own obfuscation."
msgstr "Sarah frunció el ceño. La frustraba cuánto disfrutaba el espíritu de su propia evasiva."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "And yet you want me to trust you."
msgstr "Y, sin embargo, quieres que confíe en ti."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The creature turned its mask to her."
msgstr "La criatura le giró la máscara hacia ella."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Trust..."
msgstr "Confianza..."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "No...mutual need. Similar goals. A convergence of interests."
msgstr "No... necesidad mutua. Objetivos similares. Una convergencia de intereses."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Our fates are bound to one another. And we play for the greatest of stakes."
msgstr "Nuestros destinos están ligados entre sí. Y jugamos con la mayor de las apuestas."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah idly nodded."
msgstr "Sarah asintió distraídamente."

msgctxt "speaker:Sarah"
msgid "Yes, you've told me as much. Gods and whatnot."
msgstr "Sí, eso ya me lo has dicho. Dioses y todo eso."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "The spirit drew closer and the tone of its voice shifted."
msgstr "El espíritu se acercó más y el tono de su voz cambió."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "Jest if you like."
msgstr "Es broma, si quieres."

msgctxt "speaker:Razaphel"
msgid "But failure means that we shall share a fate worse than any you can conjure."
msgstr "Pero el fracaso significa que compartiremos un destino peor que cualquiera que puedas conjurar."

msgctxt "speaker:Narrator"
msgid "Sarah felt a cold chill run down her spine as the creature spoke."
